        "content": "<p>dhil opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14085\">PR #14085</a> from <code>dhil:switch-type-index</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I came across this bug whilst working on fixing the interaction between GC and stack switching. I have hoisted it here as tiny self-contained PR.</p>\n<p>The translation of <code>switch</code> would erroneously decompose a <code>ModuleInternedTypeIndex</code> and use its <code>u32</code> representation to build a <code>TypeIndex</code>. The two index types map different spaces, consequently it is possible to cause a compiler crash (out of bounds on lookup) or worse a runtime crash (argument types mismatch).<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
